    {
      "id": "post-details-1",
      "name": "Classic Centered Article",
      "description": "Elegant typography focused layout, optimized for distraction-free reading.",
      "html": "\n                        <style>\n                          .pd1-wrap{padding:100px 20px;background:#fff;font-family:serif;}\n                          .pd1-container{max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;}\n                          .pd1-meta{text-align:center;color:#6b7280;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:14px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:20px;}\n                          .pd1-title{text-align:center;color:#111;font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,56px);font-weight:900;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 40px 0;font-family:sans-serif;}\n                          .pd1-hero{width:100%;height:450px;background:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499750310107-5fef28a66643?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop') center/cover;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:50px;}\n                          .pd1-content p{color:#374151;font-size:20px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 30px 0;}\n                          .pd1-content p:first-of-type::first-letter{font-size:80px;float:left;line-height:60px;padding-right:15px;color:#111;font-weight:900;margin-top:10px;}\n                          @media(max-width:768px){.pd1-wrap{padding:50px 20px;} .pd1-hero{height:250px;} .pd1-content p{font-size:18px;}}\n                        </style>\n                        <section class=\"pd1-wrap\">\n                            <div class=\"pd1-container\">\n                                <div class=\"pd1-meta\">Design &bull; 8 Min Read</div>\n                                <h1 class=\"pd1-title\">The Philosophy of Minimalist Web Design in 2026</h1>\n                                <div class=\"pd1-hero\"></div>\n                                <div class=\"pd1-content\">\n                                    <p>Minimalism is no longer just a trend; it is a fundamental shift in how we approach digital experiences. By stripping away the non-essential, designers are able to focus the user's attention exactly where it needs to be. This philosophy creates interfaces that are not only beautiful but highly functional.</p>\n                                    <p>The core tenet of modern minimalism relies heavily on typography and whitespace. When you have fewer elements on the screen, the elements that remain must carry more weight. Large, bold headings paired with highly legible body text create a visual hierarchy that guides the reader effortlessly through the content.</p>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </section>\n                    "
    },
    {
      "id": "post-details-2",
      "name": "Split Header Article",
      "description": "Modern split layout where title and image sit side-by-side.",
      "html": "\n                        <style>\n                          .pd2-wrap{font-family:sans-serif;background:#fafafa;}\n                          .pd2-header{display:flex;min-height:500px;}\n                          .pd2-h-left{flex:1;padding:80px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;background:#111;color:#fff;}\n                          .pd2-h-right{flex:1;background:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?q=80&w=1000&auto=format&fit=crop') center/cover;}\n                          .pd2-title{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,48px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.2;margin:20px 0 30px 0;}\n                          .pd2-author{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:15px;}\n                          .pd2-avatar{width:50px;height:50px;border-radius:50%;background:#ddd;}\n                          .pd2-body{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 20px;}\n                          .pd2-body p{font-size:18px;color:#444;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 25px 0;}\n                          @media(max-width:900px){.pd2-header{flex-direction:column;min-height:auto;} .pd2-h-left{padding:50px 20px;} .pd2-h-right{height:300px;}}\n                        </style>\n                        <section class=\"pd2-wrap\">\n                            <header class=\"pd2-header\">\n                                <div class=\"pd2-h-left\">\n                                    <span style=\"color:#3b82f6;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:13px;\">Development</span>\n                                    <h1 class=\"pd2-title\">Mastering Modern JavaScript Frameworks</h1>\n                                    <div class=\"pd2-author\">\n                                        <div class=\"pd2-avatar\" style=\"background:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573497019940-1c28c88b4f3e?q=80&w=150&auto=format&fit=crop') center/cover;\"></div>\n                                        <div><div style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:15px;\">Sarah Jenkins</div><div style=\"color:#aaa;font-size:13px;\">October 12, 2026</div></div>\n                                    </div>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"pd2-h-right\"></div>\n                            </header>\n                            <article class=\"pd2-body\">\n                                <p>Building web applications today requires a deep understanding of component-driven architectures. Whether you are using React, Vue, or Svelte, the principles remain largely the same: state management, lifecycle hooks, and optimized rendering.</p>\n                                <p>In this comprehensive guide, we dive deep into advanced patterns that will help you scale your frontend codebase without sacrificing performance or developer experience.</p>\n                            </article>\n                        </section>\n                    "
    },
    {
      "id": "post-details-3",
      "name": "Dark Tech Article",
      "description": "A sleek dark mode design perfect for coding and tech blogs.",
      "html": "\n                        <style>\n                          .pd3-wrap{padding:80px 20px;background:#09090b;font-family:sans-serif;}\n                          .pd3-container{max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;}\n                          .pd3-tag{display:inline-block;padding:6px 14px;background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);color:#818cf8;border:1px solid rgba(99,102,241,0.2);border-radius:20px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:20px;}\n                          .pd3-title{color:#fff;font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,52px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 30px 0;}\n                          .pd3-meta{color:#71717a;font-size:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:15px;margin-bottom:50px;padding-bottom:30px;border-bottom:1px solid #27272a;}\n                          .pd3-content p{color:#a1a1aa;font-size:18px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 25px 0;}\n                          .pd3-code{background:#18181b;border:1px solid #27272a;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;color:#34d399;font-family:monospace;font-size:15px;overflow-x:auto;margin:30px 0;}\n                          @media(max-width:768px){.pd3-wrap{padding:40px 20px;}}\n                        </style>\n                        <section class=\"pd3-wrap\">\n                            <div class=\"pd3-container\">\n                                <span class=\"pd3-tag\">TUTORIAL</span>\n                                <h1 class=\"pd3-title\">Building a High-Performance API with Rust</h1>\n                                <div class=\"pd3-meta\">\n                                    <span>By David Chen</span><span>&bull;</span><span>Nov 5, 2026</span><span>&bull;</span><span>12 Min Read</span>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"pd3-content\">\n                                    <p>Rust has quickly become the language of choice for systems programming and highly concurrent web services. Its memory safety guarantees without a garbage collector make it incredibly fast and reliable.</p>\n                                    <p>Let's look at how we can bootstrap a simple HTTP server using the Actix-Web framework:</p>\n                                    <div class=\"pd3-code\">\nuse actix_web::{get, App, HttpServer, Responder};\n\n#[get(\"/\")]\nasync fn hello() -> impl Responder {\n    \"Hello, world!\"\n}\n                                    </div>\n                                    <p>This simple snippet is capable of handling hundreds of thousands of requests per second. The zero-cost abstractions in Rust mean you don't pay for features you don't use.</p>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </section>\n                    "
    },
    {
      "id": "post-details-4",
      "name": "Hero Image Overlay",
      "description": "Immersive full-screen background image with text overlay.",
      "html": "\n                        <style>\n                          .pd4-wrap{font-family:sans-serif;background:#fff;}\n                          .pd4-hero{height:80vh;min-height:500px;background:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469474968028-56623f02e42e?q=80&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop') center/cover;position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:20px;}\n                          .pd4-overlay{position:absolute;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,0.5);}\n                          .pd4-hero-content{position:relative;z-index:1;max-width:900px;}\n                          .pd4-title{color:#fff;font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);font-weight:900;line-height:1.1;margin:0 0 20px 0;text-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);}\n                          .pd4-subtitle{color:#e2e8f0;font-size:clamp(18px,2.5vw,24px);font-weight:400;text-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);}\n                          .pd4-body{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 20px;}\n                          .pd4-body p{font-size:20px;color:#333;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 30px 0;}\n                        </style>\n                        <section class=\"pd4-wrap\">\n                            <header class=\"pd4-hero\">\n                                <div class=\"pd4-overlay\"></div>\n                                <div class=\"pd4-hero-content\">\n                                    <h1 class=\"pd4-title\">The Ultimate Guide to Sustainable Travel</h1>\n                                    <p class=\"pd4-subtitle\">How to explore the world without leaving a trace.</p>\n                                </div>\n                            </header>\n                            <article class=\"pd4-body\">\n                                <p>Traveling opens our minds to new cultures, cuisines, and landscapes. However, the environmental impact of global tourism cannot be ignored. Sustainable travel is about making simple choices that lessen your negative impact on a given destination.</p>\n                                <p>From choosing eco-friendly accommodations to supporting local artisans rather than multinational chains, every decision counts. This guide will walk you through practical steps to become a more responsible global citizen while exploring our beautiful planet.</p>\n                            </article>\n                        </section>\n                    "
    },
